</figure></div></div>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F19" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/PlotKeywordDistribOverTime.svg" id="A3.F19.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/206;" width="476" height="206"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F19.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 19</span>: </span><span id="A3.F19.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Distribution of all <span id="A3.F19.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Migrant</span> keywords over the years, normalized per keyword. The keywords are sorted by frequency, which means that the reliability decreases towards the bottom-right.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F20" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/1867-2025_PerKeywordAndDecade.svg" id="A3.F20.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/206;" width="476" height="206"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F20.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 20</span>: </span><span id="A3.F20.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Percentage of sentences showing solidarity/anti-solidarity per decade for all <span id="A3.F20.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Migrant</span> keywords from 1867 to 2025. The keywords are sorted by frequency, which means that the reliability decreases towards the bottom-right.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F21" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/Migrant_Onestep_prompt.svg" id="A3.F21.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:381/535;" width="381" height="535"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F21.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 21</span>: </span><span id="A3.F21.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">One-step zero-shot prompt set used for the evaluation of GPT-4 on the <em id="A3.F21.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Migrant</em> dataset.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F22" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/Frau_Onestep_prompt.svg" id="A3.F22.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:381/531;" width="381" height="531"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F22.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 22</span>: </span><span id="A3.F22.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">One-step zero-shot prompt set used for the evaluation of GPT-4 on the <em id="A3.F22.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Frau</em> dataset.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F23" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F23.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/MostGeneralKeywords_Finegrained.svg" id="A3.F23.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:272/111;" width="272" height="111"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F23.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F23.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/MostGeneralKeywords_Highlevel.svg" id="A3.F23.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:176/112;" width="176" height="112"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F23.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F23.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 23</span>: </span><span id="A3.F23.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(Anti-)solidarity trends in 1867-2022, restricted to the keywords <em id="A3.F23.9.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Flüchtlinge</em> and <em id="A3.F23.9.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Ausländer</em>. Figure <a href="#A3.F23.sf1" title="In Figure 23 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23(a)</span></a> shows the fraction of solidarity (left) and anti-solidarity (right) subtypes predicted by Llama-3.3-70B. <span id="A3.F23.9.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Percentages are normalized within each decade across all eight subtypes, so the curves in both panels together sum to 100% per decade.</span> Figure <a href="#A3.F23.sf2" title="In Figure 23 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23(b)</span></a> shows the aggregated proportions of solidarity, anti-solidarity, and mixed labels per decade; <span id="A3.F23.9.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">totals may not reach 100% because instances classified as <span id="A3.F23.9.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote">“None”</span> are omitted (though included in the calculation).</span> The period from 1933 to 1949 <span id="A3.F23.9.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(grey shaded area)</span> is excluded due to limited data availability during and immediately after the NS dictatorship.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F24" class="ltx_figure">
<figure id="A3.F24.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/Migrant_High-Level-Prompt.svg" id="A3.F24.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/302;" width="476" height="302"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F24.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A3.F24.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">High-level prompt (Step 1).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F24.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 24</span>: </span><span id="A3.F24.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Two-step few-shot prompt set used for the evaluation of open-weight models on the <em id="A3.F24.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Migrant</em> dataset and for the final large-scale annotation with Llama-3.3-70B.
The model is first given the high-level classification prompt in Figure <a href="#A3.F27.sf1" title="In Figure 27 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27(a)</span></a>.
If the output is Solidarity or Anti-solidarity, the corresponding subtype prompt in Subfigure <a href="#A3.F28.sf1" title="In Figure 28 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28(a)</span></a> or Subfigure <a href="#A3.F29.sf1" title="In Figure 29 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29(a)</span></a> is used.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F25" class="ltx_figure">
<figure id="A3.F25.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/Migrant-Solidarity-Prompt.svg" id="A3.F25.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/350;" width="476" height="350"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F25.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A3.F25.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Subtype prompt for Solidarity (Step 2a).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F25.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 25</span>: </span><span id="A3.F25.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Two-step few-shot prompt set used for the evaluation of open-weight models on the <em id="A3.F25.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Migrant</em> dataset and for the final large-scale annotation with Llama-3.3-70B (continued from Fig. <a href="#A3.F24" title="Figure 24 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F26" class="ltx_figure">
<figure id="A3.F26.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/Migrant-Anti-Solidarity-Prompt.svg" id="A3.F26.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/381;" width="476" height="381"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F26.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A3.F26.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Subtype prompt for Anti-solidarity (Step 2b).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F26.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 26</span>: </span><span id="A3.F26.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Two-step few-shot prompt set used for the evaluation of open-weight models on the <em id="A3.F26.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Migrant</em> dataset and for the final large-scale annotation with Llama-3.3-70B (continued from Fig. <a href="#A3.F24" title="Figure 24 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F27" class="ltx_figure">
<figure id="A3.F27.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.07274v1/Frau-Highlevel-Prompt.svg" id="A3.F27.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/324;" width="476" height="324"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F27.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A3.F27.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">High-level prompt (Step 1).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F27.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 27</span>: </span><span id="A3.F27.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Two-step few-shot prompt set used for the evaluation of open-weight models on the <em id="A3.F27.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Frau</em> dataset. The model is first given the high-level classification prompt in Figure <a href="#A3.F27.sf1" title="In Figure 27 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27(a)</span></a>.
If the output is Solidarity or Anti-solidarity, the corresponding subtype prompt in Subfigure <a href="#A3.F28.sf1" title="In Figure 28 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28(a)</span></a> or Subfigure <a href="#A3.F29.sf1" title="In Figure 29 ‣ Fine-Tuned Llama Models ‣ Appendix C Models Inference and Training Details ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29(a)</span></a> is used.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
