<td id="A3.T6.3.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">63</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.11.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.11.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.11.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.11.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.11.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.11.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.11.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">33</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.11.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.11.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.11.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.3.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">None</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">81</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1564</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">78</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">389</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">94</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">54</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">754</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">47</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.12.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="A3.T6.3.12.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T6.3.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Total per party</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">300</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3394</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">203</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">41</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">46</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">882</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">369</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">226</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2241</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">263</span></td>
<td id="A3.T6.3.13.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T6.3.13.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T6.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A3.T6.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Distribution of (anti-)solidarity subtypes by party included in the post-war trends analysis (Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Germany after the Second World War, 1949-1957 ‣ 4 Temporal Trends in Solidarity Towards Migrants ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>). AS stands for Anti-Solidarity; S for Solidarity.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T7" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T7.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T7.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T7.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T7.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Original Text</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T7.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Translation</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T7.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T7.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(1) </span><span id="A3.T7.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based solidarity towards expellees
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T7.3.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(May 14, 1952)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] das Lastenausgleichsgesetz und die Eingliederung der Vertriebenen [steht] in keinem Widerspruch zu unserm Anspruch und unserm Recht auf die Heimat. <span id="A3.T7.3.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Im Gegenteil, […] daß die Rücksiedlung […] nur durchgeführt werden kann, wenn die körperliche, seelische und auch die wirtschaftliche Substanz der Vertriebenen erhalten geblieben ist, und das kann nur geschehen, wenn sie in die westdeutsche Wirtschaft eingegliedert werden.</span> […] Wir sind durchaus für die Ausgestaltung des Lastenausgleichs nach sozialen Gesichtspunkten; […] aber der Rechtsanspruch darf nicht so behandelt werden, als sei er nur etwas Zweitrangiges, angewiesen auf das, was übrigbleibt.”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] the Equalization of Burdens Act and the integration of the expellees does not contradict our right to the homeland. <span id="A3.T7.3.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">On the contrary, resettlement […] can only be achieved if the physical, mental, and economic substance of the expellees has been preserved, and that can only happen if they are integrated into the West German economy.</span> […] We are fully in favor of shaping the Equalization of Burdens in accordance with social considerations; […] but the legal entitlement should not be treated as secondary, dependent only on what is left over.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T7.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T7.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(2) </span><span id="A3.T7.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: exchange-based solidarity towards expellees
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T7.3.3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Feb 25, 1953)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Ich darf […] auf einige Gesichtspunkte hinweisen […] zum Bundesvertriebenengesetz. <span id="A3.T7.3.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Der Ihnen vorliegende Entwurf geht […] von der Zielsetzung aus, die […] Leistungskraft der Vertriebenen und Flüchtlinge […] im Rahmen der Gesamtwirtschaft zur Geltung zu bringen.</span> Die Eingliederungsbestimmungen sollen der Erfüllung berechtigter Ausgleichsansprüche hinsichtlich der verlorenen Existenz dienen […] mit dem Ziel, daß sich das gesamte Arbeitspotential, das der Einheimischen und der Vertriebenen, so betätigen kann, daß eine größtmögliche Wirkung erzielt wird.”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“I would like to point out some aspects […] on the Federal Expellees Act. <span id="A3.T7.3.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The draft before you starts from the objective […] of making […] productive capacities of the expellees and refugees […] effective within the overall economy.</span> The integration provisions are intended to meet legitimate compensation claims with regard to lost livelihoods […] with the goal that the entire labor potential, that of natives and of expellees alike, can be deployed in such a way that the greatest possible effect is achieved.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T7.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T7.3.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(3) </span><span id="A3.T7.3.4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: compassionate solidarity towards Soviet-zone refugees
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T7.3.4.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(June 15, 1955)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] <span id="A3.T7.3.4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">es ist notwendig, zu den noch immer vielseitigen Problemen der Sowjetzonenflüchtlinge Stellung zu nehmen […].</span> Wir erkennen selbstverständlich an, daß durch die Neuregelung des Härtefonds im Lastenausgleich eine Verbesserung für die Sowjetzonenflüchtlinge erfolgte, weil die Ermessensfragen, unter denen dieser Personenkreis bislang besonders zu leiden hatte, dadurch eingeschränkt werden. […] Wenn wir aber die Sicherheit haben wollen, daß sich diese Neuregelung auch wirklich positiv für den Flüchtling auswirkt, so ist es notwendig, daß die vorgesehene Erhöhung des Härtefonds […] wirklich realisiert wird.”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] <span id="A3.T7.3.4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">it is necessary to address the still manifold problems of the Soviet-zone refugees […].</span> We naturally recognize that the reform of the hardship fund in the Equalization of Burdens has brought improvements […] because the discretionary decisions that this group had particularly suffered from have been curtailed. But if we want to be sure that this reform really has a positive effect for the refugee, then […] the planned increase of the hardship fund […] must actually be implemented.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T7.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T7.3.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(4) </span><span id="A3.T7.3.5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards expellees
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T7.3.5.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Dec 13, 1950)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“In unseren Landkreisverwaltungen sind heute 42,2% Heimatvertriebene. […] Auch die einheimische Bevölkerung beklagt sich […] man höre auf den Landratsämtern überwiegend ostpreußisch, und das Plattdeutsche sei zur Seite gedrängt. Unter den Lehrern […] 51% Heimatvertriebene, unter den vollbeschäftigten Richtern […] mehr als 50%, unter der Polizei sogar 61%; zweifellos eine Überfremdung, die Besorgnis erregt! <span id="A3.T7.3.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Aber all diese ehrlichen Bemühungen um Eingliederung der Heimatvertriebenen sind angesichts der ungeheuren Zahl vergeblich.</span> Arbeitslosenzahl […] beträgt unter den Heimatvertriebenen fast 60%. Die Lasten sind unerschwinglich.”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T7.3.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T7.3.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.3.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“In our district administrations today, 42.2% are expellees. The native population […] complains […] that in the district offices one mostly hears East Prussian, and that Low German has been pushed aside. Among the teachers 51% are expellees, among the full-time judges also more than 50%, among the police even 61% – undoubtedly an over-foreignization that arouses concern! <span id="A3.T7.3.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">But all these honest efforts to integrate the expellees are in vain in view of their immense numbers.</span> Unemployment […] almost 60% among the expellees […]. The burdens are unbearable.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 7</span>: </span><span id="A3.T7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples for postwar period discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Germany after the Second World War, 1949-1957 ‣ 4 Temporal Trends in Solidarity Towards Migrants ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. Bold text is the main sentence, the other sentences are for context.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T8" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T8.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T8.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T8.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T8.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Original Text</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T8.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Translation</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T8.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T8.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(5) </span><span id="A3.T8.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based solidarity towards Soviet-zone refugees
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T8.3.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Sept 23, 1954)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] den Ländern [wurden] für die wohnungsmäßige Unterbringung der […] Sowjetzonenflüchtlinge […] 350 Millionen DM […] zur Verfügung gestellt […]. <span id="A3.T8.3.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Der Bundestag ist […] davon ausgegangen, daß die Sowjetzonenflüchtlinge im Lastenausgleich nicht berücksichtigt werden konnten und daß die Verweisung […] auf den Härtefonds nur als Interimslösung gedacht war.</span> […] Die Bundesregierung prüft […] noch […] Maßnahmen, um den bei den Sowjetzonenflüchtlingen auftretenden Notständen abzuhelfen.”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] the federal government provided 350 million DM for the housing of […] Soviet-zone refugees […]. <span id="A3.T8.3.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parliament assumed that Soviet-zone refugees could not be included in the Equalization of Burdens and that referral […] to the hardship fund was intended only as an interim solution.</span> […] The federal government is still examining measures to address the emergencies arising among the Soviet-zone refugees.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T8.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T8.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(6) </span><span id="A3.T8.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards foreigners
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T8.3.3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(June 21, 1956)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] Wir müssen das Bundesgebiet nicht nur gegen politisch subversive Elemente, <span id="A3.T8.3.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">wir müssen uns auch gegen kriminelle Elemente abschirmen</span>. […] <span id="A3.T8.3.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Für die Bundesrepublik kommt […] hinzu, daß sie […] Anlaß hat, sich gegen Zehntausende von heimatlosen Ausländern abzuschirmen, die […] in der Absicht [kommen], bei uns wirtschaftliche Versorgung oder politisches Asyl zu finden.</span> […] alle internationalen Verpflichtungen, die wir […] erfüllen, [gehören] selbstverständlich nicht unter das, was ich hier ausgeführt habe.”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] We must shield the Federal territory not only against politically subversive elements, <span id="A3.T8.3.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">we but also against criminal elements</span>. […] <span id="A3.T8.3.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">For the Federal Republic there is the added circumstance that it has reason to shield itself against tens of thousands of stateless foreigners who […] come with the intention of seeking economic support or political asylum here.</span> […] all international obligations which we […] fulfill, of course, do not fall under what I have set out here.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T8.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T8.3.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(7) </span><span id="A3.T8.3.4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based solidarity towards foreigners
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T8.3.4.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Oct 18, 1950)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] Auch in der öffentlichen Fürsorge sollen sie Leistungen in gleicher Höhe erhalten wie deutsche Staatsangehörige. Es soll ihnen Zutritt zu Schulen aller Art zu den gleichen Bedingungen wie Deutschen gewährt werden. […] die Bundesrepublik [gewährt] ihnen einen Rechtsschutz, dessen sie bedürfen, weil sie nicht mehr den Schutz ihres Heimatstaates genießen […]. <span id="A3.T8.3.4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Der Gesetzentwurf geht […] über den Konventionsentwurf, dessen Grundsätze Mindestforderungen für die Behandlung heimatloser Ausländer darstellen, hinaus. […]</span>”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] In public welfare too, they are to receive benefits equal to those of German citizens. They are to be granted access to schools of all kinds under the same conditions as Germans. […] the Federal Republic shall grant them legal protection, which they need because they no longer enjoy the protection of their home state […]. <span id="A3.T8.3.4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The draft law goes […] beyond the draft convention, whose principles set minimum standards for the treatment of stateless foreigners. […]</span>”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T8.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T8.3.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(8) </span><span id="A3.T8.3.5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based solidarity towards foreigners
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T8.3.5.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(April 19, 1951)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] <span id="A3.T8.3.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wir begrüßen die Verabschiedung des Gesetzes für heimatlose Ausländer, weil uns damit die Möglichkeit geboten war, dem Ausland zu beweisen, wie wir Angehörige anderer Nationen in unserem eigenen Staate zu behandeln gewillt sind, und weil wir uns […] erhoffen, daß sie […] dazu beitragen wird, die Frage der Internationalisierung unseres Flüchtlingsproblems und des Zuflusses von Mitteln aus dem Ausland zu fördern.</span> […]”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] <span id="A3.T8.3.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We welcome the adoption of the law for stateless foreigners, because it gave us the opportunity to demonstrate to foreign countries how we intend to treat nationals of other nations within our own state, and because we […] hope that it will make a contribution to promoting the internationalization of our refugee problem and the inflow of funds from abroad.</span> […]”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.3.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T8.3.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T8.3.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(9) </span><span id="A3.T8.3.6.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: empathic solidarity towards foreigners
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T8.3.6.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(June 15, 1955)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] <span id="A3.T8.3.6.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Es ist kein Zweifel, daß die heimatlosen Ausländer natürlich vom Arbeitsministerium und vom Innenministerium […] eine rein materielle Unterstützung bekommen.</span> Aber diese materielle Unterstützung gibt keine Möglichkeit, ihnen kulturell oder sonstwie unter die Arme zu greifen. […] [Es ist sehr schwer] diese Dinge heute den Ländern nahezulegen.”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T8.3.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T8.3.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T8.3.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T8.3.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] <span id="A3.T8.3.6.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">There is no doubt that the stateless foreigners, of course, receive […] purely material support from the Ministry of Labor and the Ministry of the Interior.</span> But this material support provides no opportunity to assist them culturally or in other ways. […] [It is very difficult] today to persuade the Länder on these matters. […]”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="A3.T8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples for postwar period discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Germany after the Second World War, 1949-1957 ‣ 4 Temporal Trends in Solidarity Towards Migrants ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> (continued). Bold text is the main sentence, the other sentences are for context.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T9" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T9.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T9.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T9.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T9.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Original Text</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T9.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Translation</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T9.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T9.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T9.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(10) </span><span id="A3.T9.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: exchange-based solidarity towards expellees,
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: FDP
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T9.3.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Oct 20, 1949)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Die werden […] von früh morgens bis spät abends arbeiten, wenn man ihnen das nötige Gelände, [Baumaterialien oder das Geld] zur Verfügung stellt. So werden sie in Gemeinschaftsarbeit wesentlich mehr leisten, als wir das sonst heute bei diesen Bauten sehen. In diesem Falle wäre das Geld, das wir dafür aufnehmen, praktisch nur als Kredit anzusehen. <span id="A3.T9.3.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wir hätten die Möglichkeit, daß diese Heimatvertriebenen sich ihr Heim selbst bauen, daß es allmählich ihr Eigentum wird.</span> Wenn wir nur normale Mietsätze verrechnen und das Kapital ohne Zinsen oder zu geringen Zinssätzen verzinsen lassen, so wäre in wenigen, spätestens 15 Jahren, dieses Haus […] Eigentum des Betreffenden. ”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“They would […] work from early morning until late at night if they were provided with the necessary land, [building materials or the money]. In cooperative work they would achieve far more than we otherwise see with such construction today. <span id="A3.T9.3.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">In this case the money we raise would practically only be regarded as a loan.</span> We would have the possibility that these expellees build their homes themselves, gradually becoming their property. If we only charged normal rents and let the capital bear no or low interest, then within at most fifteen years this house […] would become the property of the person concerned.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T9.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T9.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T9.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(11) </span><span id="A3.T9.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based solidarity towards expellees,
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: GB/BHE
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T9.3.3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Oct 29, 1953)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] <span id="A3.T9.3.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wir dürfen die Augen auch nicht vor der Tatsache verschließen, daß Millionen von Vertriebenen und Kriegsgeschädigten noch nicht den Anschluß an unsere soziale Entwicklung gefunden haben.</span> Auch hier mußten bisher Zehntausende arbeitswilliger tüchtiger Mitbürger abseitsstehen. Bei unserem Verlangen nach beschleunigter Eingliederung dieser Bevölkerungskreise geht es nicht nur um die Ablösung einer unproduktiven Fürsorge durch aufbauende Mitarbeit. Es geht auch nicht nur um die Erfüllung von <span id="A3.T9.3.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘Rechtsansprüchen’</span>, und ich darf diesen Ausdruck Rechtsansprüche hier noch einmal betonen.
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] <span id="A3.T9.3.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We must not close our eyes to the fact that millions of expellees and war victims have still not been integrated into our social development.</span> Here too, tens of thousands of willing and capable fellow citizens have so far had to stand aside. In our demand for the accelerated integration of these groups, it is not only a matter of replacing unproductive welfare with constructive participation. It is also not only a matter of fulfilling legal claims — and I would like to emphasize this expression <span id="A3.T9.3.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘legal claims’</span> once again.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T9.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T9.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T9.3.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(12) </span><span id="A3.T9.3.4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: compassionate solidarity towards refugees,
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: WAV
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T9.3.4.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(March 23, 1950)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Die Aufnahme dieser Flüchtlinge wird in manchen Ländern bewußt erschwert, sabotiert und unmöglich gemacht. […] <span id="A3.T9.3.4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Seitdem die Spannung zwischen Osten und Westen zunimmt, hat ein neuer Strom von Flüchtlingen eingesetzt.</span> […] Polen und die Tschechei [durchführen] die neue Ausweisungsaktion auf Befehl Moskaus, […] um das Flüchtlingsheer in Westdeutschland zu vermehren und noch mehr Arbeitslose zu schaffen, den Staat zu belasten und seine Wirtschaft zu zerstören. […]”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“The admission of these refugees is being deliberately obstructed, sabotaged, and made impossible in some states. […] <span id="A3.T9.3.4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Since the tension between East and West has increased, a new stream of refugees has begun.</span> […] Poland and Czechoslovakia are carrying out the new expulsions on orders from Moscow, […] in order to enlarge the refugee army in West Germany, to create even more unemployed, to burden the state, and to destroy its economy. […]”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T9.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T9.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T9.3.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(13) </span><span id="A3.T9.3.5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards expellees,
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: BP
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T9.3.5.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Oct 20, 1949)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Die Sudetendeutschen […] und die Südostdeutschen [stehen] dem süddeutschen, also dem bayerischen Kulturkreis am nächsten. […] Die aus dem Sudetenland bzw. aus Südosteuropa kommenden Deutschen [sollen] zunächst in Süddeutschland zusammen[gefasst werden], […] damit die Eingliederung […] schneller und reibungsloser vor sich gehen kann. <span id="A3.T9.3.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[Wir] wollen […] nicht Schwierigkeiten schaffen, wo Schwierigkeiten nicht überwunden werden müssen, und nicht Gräben aufreißen, wo solche nicht vorhanden sind.</span> Das hat mit Rassentheorie […] gar nichts zu tun. […] ”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.3.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T9.3.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T9.3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T9.3.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“The Sudeten Germans […] and the Southeast Germans are closest to the South German, that is, the Bavarian cultural sphere. […] The Germans coming from the Sudetenland and from Southeastern Europe [should] initially be concentrated in southern Germany, […] so that integration […] can proceed more quickly and smoothly. <span id="A3.T9.3.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[…] we do not want to create difficulties where difficulties need not arise, and we do not want to open up rifts where none exist.</span> This has nothing to do with racial theory […]. ”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 9</span>: </span><span id="A3.T9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples for postwar period discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Germany after the Second World War, 1949-1957 ‣ 4 Temporal Trends in Solidarity Towards Migrants ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> (continued). Bold text is the main sentence, the other sentences are for context.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T10" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T10.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T10.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T10.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A3.T10.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T10.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T10.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T10.3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Original Text</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T10.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T10.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T10.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T10.3.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Translation</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T10.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T10.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T10.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T10.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T10.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(14) </span><span id="A3.T10.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based solidarity towards refugees,
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: KPD
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T10.3.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Dec 13, 1950)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T10.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T10.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T10.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T10.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Wir glauben, daß das Problem der Beschaffung von Arbeit für [Umsiedler] unter dem kapitalistischen System nicht in der Form gelöst werden kann […]. Wir sind also der Auffassung, daß die Umsiedlung eine Notwendigkeit ist […]. <span id="A3.T10.3.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wenn hier der Sprecher der CDU das schöne, stolze und richtige Wort geprägt hat <span id="A3.T10.3.2.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘Unser Haus ist deutsch’</span>, wenn er am Schluß gesagt hat <span id="A3.T10.3.2.2.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘Das ganze Deutschland soll es sein’</span>, wie kann man dann […] gleichzeitig die Tatsache, daß sich die Vertriebenen, Flüchtlinge und Umsiedler, wie Sie sie bezeichnen, politisch zu Parteien zusammengeschlossen haben, als die Gefahr einer Überfremdung bezeichnen?</span>
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T10.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T10.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T10.3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T10.3.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“We believe that the problem of providing work for [resettlers] cannot be solved under the capitalist system […]. We therefore take the view that resettlement is a necessity […]. <span id="A3.T10.3.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">If the CDU speaker here has coined the fine, proud, and correct phrase <span id="A3.T10.3.2.3.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘Our house is German’</span>, and if he concluded by saying <span id="A3.T10.3.2.3.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘It shall be the whole of Germany’</span>, how then can one at the same time describe the fact that the expellees, refugees, and resettlers, as you call them, have politically organized themselves into parties as a danger of being overrun by foreigners?</span>”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 10</span>: </span><span id="A3.T10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples for postwar period discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Germany after the Second World War, 1949-1957 ‣ 4 Temporal Trends in Solidarity Towards Migrants ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> (continued). Bold text is the main sentence, the other sentences are for context.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T11" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T11.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T11.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T11.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A3.T11.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T11.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T11.3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Original Text</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T11.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T11.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T11.3.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Translation</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T11.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T11.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T11.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T11.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(15) </span><span id="A3.T11.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: compassionate solidarity towards refugees 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: Die Grünen</span><span id="A3.T11.3.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.T11.3.2.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Nov 6, 2014)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T11.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T11.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T11.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“<span id="A3.T11.3.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ich bin froh, dass es heute bei uns in Deutschland eine andere Willkommenskultur gibt und dass sich viele Menschen mit hohem Engagement für das Wohl der Flüchtlinge, die im Augenblick zu uns kommen, einsetzen.</span> […] Ich will ganz klar sagen: Das Boot ist nicht voll; das Boot ist niemals voll. Heute geht es um Grundrechte von Menschen, denen die Grundrechte in ihren Heimatländern versagt wurden […].
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T11.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T11.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T11.3.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“<span id="A3.T11.3.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">I am glad that today in Germany we have a different welcoming culture, and that many people are working with great commitment for the well-being of the refugees who are currently coming to us.</span> […] I want to state very clearly: the boat is not full; the boat is never full. Today it is about the fundamental rights of people who have been denied those rights in their home countries […].”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T11.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T11.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T11.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T11.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(16) </span><span id="A3.T11.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards refugees
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T11.3.3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Oct 1, 2015)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T11.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T11.3.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T11.3.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] Wenn die Zahlen weiterhin auf diesem hohen Niveau bleiben, dann wird Deutschland über kurz oder lang überfordert sein. Was die Registrierung, Antragstellung und Antragsbearbeitung anbelangt, ist dies eine riesige Herausforderung, und die Unterbringung sowie die Integration in unsere Gesellschaft und in den Arbeitsmarkt sind […] auf die Dauer nicht zu leisten […]. <span id="A3.T11.3.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">allein im September sind mehrere zehntausend Flüchtlinge und Asylbewerber nach Deutschland gekommen.</span> Sie wurden nicht registriert. Sie wurden nicht kontrolliert. […] Damit besteht auch ein großes Sicherheitsrisiko.
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T11.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T11.3.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T11.3.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] If the numbers remain at this high level, Germany will sooner or later be overburdened. Registration, application processing and decision-making are a huge challenge, and accommodation as well as integration into our society and the labor market will […] not be sustainable in the long run […]. <span id="A3.T11.3.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">In September alone, several tens of thousands of refugees and asylum seekers came to Germany.</span> They were not registered. They were not controlled. […] This poses a major security risk.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T11.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T11.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T11.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T11.3.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(17) </span><span id="A3.T11.3.4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: exchange-based anti-solidarity towards refugees
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: AfD
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T11.3.4.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(May 16, 2018)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T11.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T11.3.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T11.3.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“<span id="A3.T11.3.4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[…] jährlich [verlassen] etwa 140 000 Hochkompetente […] dieses Land und im Gegenzug nach derzeitigem Stand um die 200 000 sogenannte Flüchtlinge hereinkommen, von denen nicht nur kaum einer hochkompetent ist, sondern viele Analphabeten sind.</span> In Deutschland, meine Damen und Herren, lebt bereits eine große soziale Unterschicht […]. Diese Zahl wächst seit 2015 durch die Zuwanderung von Gering- und Unqualifizierten rasant. Meine Damen und Herren, Deutschland ist kein reiches Land, sondern ein leistungsfähiges.
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T11.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T11.3.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T11.3.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T11.3.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“<span id="A3.T11.3.4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">[…] each year about 140,000 highly qualified people leave this country, while in return, according to the current situation, about 200,000 so-called refugees enter, of whom hardly any are highly qualified, but many are illiterate.</span> In Germany, ladies and gentlemen, there already lives a large social underclass […]. Since 2015, this number has been growing rapidly through the immigration of low- and unqualified people. Ladies and gentlemen, Germany is not a rich country, but a capable one.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 11</span>: </span><span id="A3.T11.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples for the 2009-2025 period discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Recent German history 2009-2025 ‣ 4 Temporal Trends in Solidarity Towards Migrants ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>. Bold text is the main sentence, the other sentences are for context.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T12" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T12.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T12.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T12.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T12.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Original Text</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T12.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Translation</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T12.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T12.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T12.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(18) </span><span id="A3.T12.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards refugees
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: AfD
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T12.3.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Oct 19, 2022)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] Echte Kriegsflüchtlinge aus der Ukraine brauchen Schutz – keine Frage. Wir sagen aber Nein zu Fluchttourismus durch halb Europa, und wir sagen Nein zu bevorzugter Behandlung auf Kosten der deutschen Steuerzahler. Wir fordern daher die sofortige Abschaltung dieses Sozialstaatsmagneten, […] <span id="A3.T12.3.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wir fordern außerdem die Umstellung von Geldleistungen auf Sachleistungen für Asylbewerber, damit Migrationsanreize gesenkt werden und der Missbrauch effektiv unterbunden wird.</span> […] Und wer sich wie Frau Baerbock in erster Linie der ukrainischen Bevölkerung verpflichtet fühlt, der soll sich in der Ukraine um ein Amt bewerben, aber nicht in Deutschland.
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] Genuine war refugees from Ukraine need protection — no question. But we say no to flight tourism across half of Europe, and we say no to preferential treatment at the expense of German taxpayers. We therefore demand the immediate shutdown of this welfare magnet, […] <span id="A3.T12.3.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We also demand the switch from cash benefits to benefits in kind for asylum seekers, so that incentives for migration are reduced and abuse is effectively curbed.</span> […] And whoever, like Ms. Baerbock, feels primarily obligated to the Ukrainian population should run for office in Ukraine, but not in Germany.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T12.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T12.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T12.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(19) </span><span id="A3.T12.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards refugees
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: AfD
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T12.3.3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Dec 5, 2023)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] alte Leute sollen lieber aus ihren großen Wohnungen ausziehen, weil grün-linke Politik Millionen Gäste aus Afrika und dem Nahen Osten einlädt und gleichzeitig den Wohnungsbau abwürgt. […] <span id="A3.T12.3.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dafür werden bereits Zimmer in angeblich christlichen Altenheimen gekündigt, weil angebliche Flüchtlinge lukrativer sind, Messerzuwanderung inklusive.</span> […] Bei diesem Recht auf Wohnungstausch der Linken handelt es sich um eine Mischung aus Neid zulasten alter Leute und Zwang zulasten von Vermietern. Es ist die Fortsetzung einer inländerfeindlichen…
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] elderly people are supposed to move out of their large apartments because green-left politics invites millions of guests from Africa and the Middle East while simultaneously stifling housing construction. […] <span id="A3.T12.3.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rooms in supposedly Christian nursing homes are already being canceled because so-called refugees are more lucrative, knife migration<span id="footnote12" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">12</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">12</sup>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium" style="font-size:125%;">12</span></span>
                          
                          
                          
                        <em id="footnote12.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_medium ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:125%;">Messereinwanderung</em><span id="footnote12.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium" style="font-size:125%;">: a propagandistic term coined by the AfD implying migrants bring knife crime.</span></span></span></span></span> <span id="A3.T12.3.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">included.</span> […] This <span id="A3.T12.3.3.3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘right to apartment swaps’</span> proposed by the Left is a mixture of envy at the expense of elderly people and coercion at the expense of landlords. It is the continuation of an anti-native policy…”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T12.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T12.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T12.3.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(20) </span><span id="A3.T12.3.4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: exchange-based solidarity towards immigrants
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: FDP
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T12.3.4.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(May 25, 2023)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] Menschen, die bei uns arbeiten wollen, sollten wir eine echte Chance geben; denn viele, die an unserer Grenze ankommen, wollen ja gerade arbeiten. Wir arbeiten in der Ampel an der Reform des Fachkräfteeinwanderungsgesetzes. <span id="A3.T12.3.4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Da geht es um mehr Regulierung, gezielte Einwanderung in unseren Arbeitsmarkt.</span> Menschen aus dem Ausland sollten eine realistische Chance bekommen, zu uns zu kommen und arbeiten zu können. Das Fachkräfteeinwanderungsgesetz wird das jetzt endlich besser machen und mehr Menschen die Chance geben, die unsere Wirtschaft auch dringend braucht. […]
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] People who want to work here should be given a real chance; because many who arrive at our border actually want to work. Within the coalition we are working on reforming the Skilled Immigration Act. <span id="A3.T12.3.4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">This is about more regulation and targeted immigration into our labor market.</span> People from abroad should have a realistic chance to come to us and be able to work. The Skilled Immigration Act will now finally improve this and give more people the opportunity that our economy urgently needs. […]”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T12.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T12.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T12.3.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(21) </span><span id="A3.T12.3.5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards migrants
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: CDU/CSU
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T12.3.5.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(May 14, 2025)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] Die gute Nachricht ist: Der Politikwechsel hat begonnen. […] <span id="A3.T12.3.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Die illegale Migration der letzten zehn Jahre gefährdet die politische Stabilität Deutschlands und Europas.</span> […] Unsere Städte und Gemeinden, die Landkreise: Alle sind über dem Limit. In den Kitas, in den Schulen, auf dem Wohnungsmarkt, bei der Sicherheit an den Bahnhöfen und auf den Marktplätzen wird diese Überforderung sehr konkret. Deswegen ist es gut, dass wir gemeinsam im Koalitionsvertrag die Migrationswende vereinbart haben: mehr Rückführungen, schnellere Verfahren und, ja, ebenso die Zurückweisung an den deutschen Grenzen auch bei Asylgesuchen.
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T12.3.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T12.3.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T12.3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T12.3.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] The good news is: the policy shift has begun. […] <span id="A3.T12.3.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The illegal migration of the last ten years endangers the political stability of Germany and Europe.</span> […] Our towns and municipalities, the districts—everyone is over the limit. In day-care centers, in schools, in the housing market, in security at train stations and in marketplaces, this overburdening becomes very concrete. That is why it is good that we have agreed together in the coalition agreement on a migration turnaround: more deportations, faster procedures, and, yes, also rejections at the German borders, even in the case of asylum applications.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 12</span>: </span><span id="A3.T12.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples for the 2009-2025 period discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Recent German history 2009-2025 ‣ 4 Temporal Trends in Solidarity Towards Migrants ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> (continued). Bold text is the main sentence, the other sentences are for context.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T13" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T13.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T13.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T13.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T13.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Original Text</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T13.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Translation</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T13.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T13.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T13.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(22) </span><span id="A3.T13.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards immigrants
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: FDP
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T13.3.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Jan 30, 2025)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Das Grundrecht auf Asyl darf nicht dazu führen, dass allein ein Antrag auf Asyl zu mehreren Jahren freiem und staatlich subventioniertem Aufenthalt in Deutschland führt, wenn er völlig ohne Grundlage erfolgt. Solche Missstände müssen wir beseitigen, damit wir uns auf jene konzentrieren können, die unsere Hilfe wirklich brauchen […]. <span id="A3.T13.3.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SPD und Grüne […] wollen die illegale Einwanderung nach Deutschland kaum begrenzen und fordern lieber weiteren Familiennachzug.</span> Diesen falschen Weg ist Deutschland leider viel zu lange gegangen. […] Eine immer linkere Politik wird […] dazu führen, dass die AfD ihr teuflisches Werk immer weiter fortsetzen kann. […]
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“The fundamental right to asylum must not result in a situation where merely submitting an asylum application leads to several years of free and state-subsidized residence in Germany when it is entirely unfounded. Such abuses must be eliminated so that we can focus on those who truly need our help […]. <span id="A3.T13.3.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The SPD and the Greens […] hardly want to limit illegal immigration to Germany and instead prefer to demand further family reunification.</span> Unfortunately, Germany has followed this wrong path for far too long. […] Ever more left-leaning policies […] will only enable the AfD to continue its diabolical work […].”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T13.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T13.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T13.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(23) </span><span id="A3.T13.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards foreigners
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T13.3.3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Misclassified; true: group-based solidarity
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T13.3.3.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Party: SPD
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T13.3.3.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Apr 10, 2024)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Kommen wir zum Entwurf der AfD und zu dem, was ihn einfach grottenschlecht macht. Sie fordern, dass in allen Fällen, in denen ein Elternteil nichtdeutscher Herkunft ist, die Ausländerbehörde beteiligt wird. Nicht nur stellen Sie damit alle Ausländer/-innen unter Generalverdacht […], sondern Sie verstoßen damit auch gegen EU-Recht […]. <span id="A3.T13.3.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sie <span id="A3.T13.3.3.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘übersehen’</span> in Ihrem Entwurf, dass ein Großteil der Ausländer, die hier die Vaterschaftsanerkennung beantragen, längst eine Niederlassungserlaubnis haben.</span> Aber gut, dass Sie gegen unsere ausländischen Mitbürgerinnen und Mitbürger hetzen. Ist ja wirklich Ihr politisches Tagesgeschäft, so bedauerlich das auch ist. […]
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Let us turn to the AfD’s draft and to what makes it simply atrocious. You demand that in all cases where one parent is of non-German origin, the immigration authority must be involved. Not only does this place all foreigners under general suspicion […], but it also violates EU law […]. <span id="A3.T13.3.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">You overlook in your draft that a large proportion of the foreigners who apply here for recognition of paternity already have permanent residency.</span> But of course, it fits your agenda to agitate against our foreign fellow citizens — that is really your daily political business, as regrettable as it is. […]”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T13.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T13.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T13.3.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(24) </span><span id="A3.T13.3.4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: group-based anti-solidarity towards migrants
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: SPD
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T13.3.4.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Dec 9, 2024)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Das Sicherheitspaket, das heute hier zur Debatte steht, ist der erste Schritt, um Konsequenzen aus der furchtbaren Katastrophe in Solingen zu ziehen. Waffenverbotszonen […] helfen [aber] Waffenverbotszonen nicht. <span id="A3.T13.3.4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Deshalb brauchen wir mehr Befugnisse für das Bundeskriminalamt und das Bundesamt für Migration.</span> Sie müssen in die Lage versetzt werden, mit den öffentlich zugänglichen Informationen Straftaten zu verhindern. Das ist dringend erforderlich, und deshalb werden wir das jetzt umsetzen. Wir werden weitere Schritte veranlassen, damit ausreisepflichtige Personen unser Land verlassen.
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“The security package being debated here today is the first step toward drawing consequences from the terrible catastrophe in Solingen. Weapons prohibition zones […] do not, however, help against terrorists. <span id="A3.T13.3.4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">That is why we need more powers for the Federal Criminal Police Office and the Federal Office for Migration.</span> They must be put in a position to use publicly available information to prevent crimes. That is urgently necessary, and that is why we will now implement it. We will take further steps to ensure that persons obliged to leave the country actually leave our country.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T13.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T13.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T13.3.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(25) </span><span id="A3.T13.3.5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted: group-based anti-solidarity towards migrants
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T13.3.5.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Misclassified; true: empathic solidarity
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T13.3.5.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Party: Die Linke
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T13.3.5.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(June 5, 2025)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“[…] <span id="A3.T13.3.5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Migration wird pauschal als sicherheitspolitisches Problem dargestellt.</span> Die AfD führt die sogenannte gescheiterte Migrationspolitik in einer Liste von Krisen auf – neben dem Krieg in der Ukraine, der Coronapandemie und der hybriden Bedrohung. Damit betreibt sie eine gefährliche und spaltende Gleichsetzung. Sie erklärt das bloße Vorhandensein von Migration zur Bedrohung der inneren und äußeren Sicherheit und nennt sie in einem Atemzug mit Terrorismus, Krieg und Katastrophen.
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T13.3.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T13.3.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T13.3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T13.3.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“<span id="A3.T13.3.5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Migration is presented across the board as a security policy problem. </span>The AfD lists the so-called failed migration policy alongside the war in Ukraine, the coronavirus pandemic, and hybrid threats. In doing so, it engages in a dangerous and divisive equation. It declares the mere existence of migration to be a threat to internal and external security, mentioning it in the same breath as terrorism, war, and disasters.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 13</span>: </span><span id="A3.T13.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples for the 2009-2025 period discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Recent German history 2009-2025 ‣ 4 Temporal Trends in Solidarity Towards Migrants ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> (continued). Bold text is the main sentence, the other sentences are for context.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T14" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T14.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T14.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T14.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A3.T14.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T14.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T14.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T14.3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Original Text</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T14.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T14.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T14.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T14.3.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Translation</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T14.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T14.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T14.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T14.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T14.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(26) </span><span id="A3.T14.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: exchange-based solidarity towards immigrants
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: Die Grünen
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T14.3.2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Jan 19, 2024)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T14.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T14.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T14.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T14.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Wissenschaftliche Institute sprechen von 400 000 Menschen jedes Jahr. Darauf müssen wir die Gesellschaft und die Politik vorbereiten. Wir müssen also ohnehin die entsprechende Infrastruktur ausbauen – Wohnungen, Schulen, Kinderbetreuung. <span id="A3.T14.3.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wir brauchen gezielte Zuwanderung, und dafür haben wir das Fachkräfteeinwanderungsgesetz gemacht.</span> Aber wir wären doch mit dem Klammerbeutel gepudert, wenn wir nicht auch das Potenzial der Menschen, die aus humanitären Gründen zu uns kommen, nutzten und dafür sorgten, dass sie aus- und weitergebildet werden und Teil unserer Gesellschaft werden. Das wäre die Hauptaufgabe. Und weil wir Zuwanderung brauchen, brauchen wir eine Willkommenskultur.
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T14.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T14.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T14.3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T14.3.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Scientific institutes speak of 400,000 people every year. Society and politics must be prepared for that. We therefore have to expand the relevant infrastructure anyway — housing, schools, childcare. <span id="A3.T14.3.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We need targeted immigration, and for that we created the Skilled Workers Immigration Act.</span> But we would have to be out of our minds not to also make use of the potential of people who come to us for humanitarian reasons, and ensure that they receive education and training and become part of our society. That would be the main task. And because we need immigration, we need a culture of welcome.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T14.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T14.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T14.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T14.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.T14.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(27) </span><span id="A3.T14.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Predicted label: empathic solidarity towards migrants
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Party: Die Linke
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.T14.3.3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(Jan 30, 2025)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T14.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T14.3.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T14.3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T14.3.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“Sie sagen, Sie wollen Frauen und Kinder schützen. Sie wollen Kinder und Frauen in Kriegsgebiete abschieben. So ist es. <span id="A3.T14.3.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wir führen eine Debatte über Sicherheit und Migration.</span> Und leider erklären alle Parteien außer der Linken, dass sie mit Abschottung dieses Land sicherer machen wollen, und reden von <span id="A3.T14.3.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘Abschiebungen im großen Stil’</span>, als seien Migranten grundsätzlich eine Gefahr. So werden Menschen unter Generalverdacht gestellt. Weniger Migration mache das Land sicherer, das ist doch Unsinn.
”</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T14.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T14.3.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T14.3.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T14.3.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_outerquote" style="font-size:80%;">“You say you want to protect women and children. You want to deport children and women to war zones. That is the reality. <span id="A3.T14.3.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We are having a debate about security and migration.</span> And unfortunately, all parties except the Left declare that they want to make this country safer through isolation, and talk about <span id="A3.T14.3.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-quote ltx_innerquote">‘deportations on a large scale,’</span> as if migrants were inherently a danger. In this way, people are placed under general suspicion. Less migration makes the country safer — that is nonsense.”</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 14</span>: </span><span id="A3.T14.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples for the 2009-2025 period discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Recent German history 2009-2025 ‣ 4 Temporal Trends in Solidarity Towards Migrants ‣ LLM Analysis of 150+ years of German Parliamentary Debates on Migration Reveals Shift from Post-War Solidarity to Anti-Solidarity in the Last Decade" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> (continued). Bold text is the main sentence, the other sentences are for context.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
